 68: 
 69: ## 2. The trust gaps, precisely (this is what Phases 2–8 fix)
 70: 
 71: **`ask` vs `search` today:**
 72: - `ask` (`AskCommand`) never touches the network for search — it only calls `AgentGateway.ask()` with the current selection as context. Correct separation exists in code.
 73: - `search` (`SearchCommand`) calls `SearchGateway.search()` (DuckDuckGo) and stores raw JSON in a `search`-type card; it never calls the agent.
 74: - **The gap is entirely in the UI**: `CommandConsoleModal`'s `BUILTIN_COMMANDS` list shows `ask` ("Generate study material with AI") and `search` ("Search configured web sources") as two rows with equal visual weight and no scope/web indicator, and both execute with zero preflight. A user cannot tell before running `ask` that it will *not* browse, or before running `search` that it *will*.
 75: 
 76: **False-"AI worked" fallback points (the single most important finding of this recon):**
 77: 1. **`OpenRouterAgentGateway.ask()`** (`src/frameworks/network/OpenRouterAgentGateway.ts:44-160`) — on **missing API key**, **any fetch/HTTP error**, **any JSON-parse failure**, or **an empty card array**, it silently calls `generateLocalFallback(query)`, which fabricates 4 generic template cards ("Core idea", "Why it matters", "How it works", "Common mistake") worded to sound like real answers. The caller (`AskCommand`, `ChunkCommand`, `CustomAgentCommand`) has no way to distinguish "the model really said this" from "the network died and this is a canned template" — both come back as a normal `AgentCardResponse[]`. This is the exact "false success" behavior item 5 in the brief is about. **Phase 2/8 fix**: the gateway must return a tagged result (or throw) so the use case/controller can label local-fallback output as such in the run receipt, never silently.
 78: 2. **`ChunkCommand`** catches AI failure per-source and falls back to `executeFaithfulSplit` (deterministic heading/paragraph split) — this fallback is *reasonable* (it's real, faithful, non-fabricated content) but is currently **invisible**: the resulting cards look identical to AI-chunked ones in the receipt. Needs labeling, not removal.
 79: 3. **`SearchCommand`** and `DuckDuckGoSearchGateway` — DDG gateway returns `[]` on any fetch error (swallowed), and `SearchCommand` throws `"No results found"` in that case — this one is honest (it fails loud), just needs a proper error UI state (Phase 8).
 80: 4. **`WebExtractionGateway`** throws on failure (also honest); `SourceCommand` catches that and stores the **error message itself** as the card body (`"Extraction failed for ${url}: ${err.message}"`) — this creates a real, persisted `source` card whose body is an error string with no visual distinction from real extracted content. Needs a failure-state card treatment, not a silent normal card.
 81: 
 82: **Undo, today:** there is no undo of any kind, no operation log persisted, no soft-delete. `OperationResult` (controller) is process-memory-only and only remembers the *last* run's created-card ids — enough to support "Undo last create" for exactly one step if nothing else has run since, but nothing more, and it vanishes on app restart or after the next operation. `DeleteCardInteractor`/`deleteSelection` permanently call `cardRepo.deleteCard()` with no snapshot kept anywhere.
 83: - **Safe undo strategy given current repositories** (no new storage engine): persist a bounded (e.g. last 20, or last N per workspace) `OperationRecord` log via a new `OperationLogRepository` (`AsyncStorage`-backed, same pattern as every other repo). Record: `id, commandName, workspaceId, parentId, inputCardIds, createdCardIds, updatedCardBefore[] (only cards actually mutated in place), deletedCardSnapshots[] (full Card, only for delete/ungroup ops), webUsed, searchQuery?, modelUsed?, startedAt, completedAt, summary`.
 84:   - **Undo create**: delete `createdCardIds` — but only if none of them have been "materially edited" since creation (compare current `card.body`/`title`/`fields` to the snapshot taken at record time; if changed, refuse and say why, per the spec's "do not claim undo succeeded if it only partially succeeded").
 85:   - **Undo delete**: re-`saveCard()` the `deletedCardSnapshots` — safe because `CardRepository.saveCard` is an upsert; if a same-id card already exists (recreated meanwhile), refuse.
 86:   - **Undo group/ungroup**: restore `parentId` on the affected cards from the pre-op snapshot; delete the group card `undo group` created only if no *other* card was reparented into it afterward.
 87:   - **Undo move**: restore `workspaceId`/`parentId` on affected cards from snapshot.
 88:   - This is a straightforward `AsyncStorage`-backed repository plus one new `UndoOperationInteractor` — no architecture change, fits the existing repository pattern exactly.
 89: 
 90: **Migration strategy (backwards compatibility), concretely:**
 91: - `Card`, `Workspace`, `AppSettings` are all plain JSON blobs in `AsyncStorage` under versioned-looking but unenforced keys (`learnimal_cards_v1`, etc.) with no schema version field and no migration runner today.
 92: - The existing pattern for adding a field safely is already established and battle-tested in this codebase: `Card.typeId` is optional and falls back to `Card.type`; `CardTypeDefinition` registries backfill missing built-ins on load (`loadCardTypes()` in the controller diffs stored vs. `BUILTIN_CARD_TYPES` and persists any that are missing). **I will follow this exact pattern**, not introduce a new migration system:
 93:   - New `Workspace.mission?: WorkspaceMission` — optional, absent = "no mission set," every read site defaults gracefully (`workspace.mission ?? undefined`), no write-time backfill needed since `undefined` round-trips through `JSON.stringify`/`parse` cleanly (unlike `null`, no special-casing needed).
 94:   - New `Card.role?: SemanticRole` — optional, additive, never replaces `Card.type`/`typeId` (per the spec's explicit requirement to keep them separate). Cards without it just don't show a role badge.
 95:   - New `Card.provenance?: Provenance` — optional, additive. Old cards simply have no provenance panel (UI shows "No provenance recorded — created before this feature" rather than fabricating one).
 96:   - New `OperationLogRepository` / `AssistantRunLog` entity — an entirely new storage key, so it starts empty; nothing to migrate.
 97:   - No existing field is renamed, removed, or changed in required-ness anywhere in this plan.
 98: 
 99: ## 3. Phase plan (files to touch, in order)
100: 
101: Each phase ends with `bun test` + `npx tsc --noEmit` (against non-test `src/`) and a commit. I will not start phase N+1 until phase N's tests are green.
102: 
103: - **Phase 0 (this document).** ✅
104: - **Phase 1 — Domain model.** `entities/workspace.ts` (+`WorkspaceMission`), `entities/card.ts` (+`role?`, +`provenance?` type import), new `entities/provenance.ts` (`Provenance`, `CreationMode`), new `entities/operationLog.ts` (`OperationRecord`), new `adapters/repositories/OperationLogRepository.ts` + `frameworks/storage/AsyncStorageOperationLogRepository.ts` + `Memory` impl. Entity-level tests only (no UI, no pipeline wiring yet).
105: - **Phase 2 — Explicit AI actions & preflight.** New `usecases/agent/AgentScope.ts` (`AgentRunRequest`), a bounded-context builder respecting max-card/char budget, 6 operation-preset request builders. New preflight bottom sheet component. Reframe `ask` in UI copy only (command stays `ask`).
106: - **Phase 3 — Web research workflow.** Normalized `ResearchResult`/`ResearchRun` types, a `ResearchInteractor` orchestrating `SearchGateway`→ (keep/reject/extract) → optional cited-synthesis `ask`, new research results screen.
107: - **Phase 4 — Mission Control + Gap Report.** Compact top-of-canvas module on `DeckScreen`/`SpaceScreen`; deterministic gap-report builder from the card graph + optional agent enrichment.
108: - **Phase 5 — Capture & selection flows.** Context-sensitive next-actions after capture; selection tray (Explain/Research/Connect/Study/More) replacing the current generic Organize/Transform.
109: - **Phase 6 — Command palette evolution.** Human-readable labels/purpose/input-output/web-indicator metadata table for all commands in `CommandConsoleModal`.
110: - **Phase 7 — Visual system.** Reduced-motion respect, HUD vocabulary pass, no new typography system (reuse `theme.ts`).
111: - **Phase 8 — Undo, error states.** `UndoOperationInteractor` per the strategy above; wire the false-fallback labeling from §2 into `AgentGateway`/`ChunkCommand`/`SourceCommand`; explicit error UI states.
112: - **Phase 9 — Tests, docs, quality gates.** Fill any coverage gaps named in the brief's acceptance list; update `README.md`/`terminal-learn-prd.md` implementation-status sections.
113: 
114: ## 4. Explicit tradeoffs taken
115: 
116: - **No new state library, no schema-migration framework** — reusing the existing optional-field + backfill-on-load pattern already proven by `cardTypes`/`promptPresets`/`assistantProfiles`.
117: - **Undo is log-based, not a general command-pattern undo stack** — bounded, per-operation, safety-checked (refuses rather than partially applying), matching the brief's "do not claim undo succeeded if it only partially succeeded."
118: - **`ask` command name is kept** (the brief says "do not remove `ask`") — only its UI framing and preflight change; scope selection is additive UI state on top of the same `AskCommand`.
119: 
120: ---
121: 
122: ## 5. Final implementation notes
123: 
124: *Written on completion. §§1–4 above were the Phase 0 reconnaissance and are left as
125: written — including predictions that turned out wrong, which are noted below.*
126: 
127: ### What shipped, by phase
128: 
129: | Phase | Outcome |
130: |---|---|
131: | 1 | `WorkspaceMission`, `Card.role`, `Card.provenance`, `OperationRecord` + `OperationLogRepository` — all additive and optional |
132: | 2 | `AgentScope` bounded-context resolution, seven operation presets, the preflight sheet |
133: | 3 | Real search via `SearchGateway`, inspectable candidates, save-as-source, cited briefs |
134: | 4 | Mission Control module, deterministic gap report, mission editor, phases |
135: | 5 | Capture receipts with next actions, the five-action selection tray |
136: | 6 | Documented command catalog, canonical actions, `/aliases` |
137: | 7 | Type scale, palettes, Google Fonts, communicative motion — plus the God-class refactor |
138: | 8 | Undo, failure cards, the global activity banner, sheet-dismissal fix |
139: | 9 | Docs and quality gates (this section) |
140: 
141: ### Corrections to the Phase 0 analysis
142: 
143: - **The undo strategy in §2 was written as if `Card` had an `updatedAt`.** It doesn't.
144:   `canUndoCreate` instead compares a content signature (title, body, answer, fields,
145:   parentId) against an as-created snapshot. This is stricter and catches edits an
146:   `updatedAt` would have missed.
147: - **The snapshot timing was subtly wrong and only caught by a test.** Snapshots were taken
148:   before auto-grouping re-parented the output, so `canUndoCreate` read the changed
149:   `parentId` as a user edit and refused *every* grouped run. Snapshots are now taken after
150:   the cards settle, and the group a run creates is part of what undo removes.
151: - **§2 predicted the trust gap was "entirely in the UI".** It was worse. Every in-flight
152:   indicator was owned by the screen that started the work, so running an action from any
153:   screen but the deck showed *nothing at all* until output silently appeared. Fixed by
154:   moving the indicator into the shell.
155: 
156: ### Migration notes
157: 
158: No migration runner was needed or written. Every field added is optional and resolves
159: through a defaulting function — `resolveAppearance`, `readFailedRunCard`, the `mission`/
160: `role`/`provenance` fields — so a settings or card blob written before this work loads
161: unchanged. `resolveGriotTheme` still honours the legacy `mode`/`accent` arguments and
162: only switches to a palette once one is explicitly chosen, so no existing user's appearance
163: changed underneath them.
164: 
165: Storage keys are unchanged except for one addition: `learnimal_operation_log_v1`, bounded
166: to the 200 most recent records.
167: 
168: ### Quality gates
169: 
170: `bun test` — 352 tests across 55 files. `npx tsc --noEmit` — clean for all non-test
171: sources. The pre-existing test-file type errors catalogued in §0 remain (missing
172: `bun-types` in `tsconfig`, plus three stale fixtures); none were introduced by this work
173: and none affect `bun test`. There is no lint configuration in the repo.
174: 
175: ### Recommended next steps
176: 
177: 1. ~~**Make `OpenRouterAgentGateway` honest.**~~ **Done.** `ask()` now returns
178:    `AgentAskResult` — cards plus `isLocalFallback` and a reason — so a caller cannot pass
179:    template content off as a model's work by accident; silence is no longer expressible in
180:    the type. Every fallback path funnels through one private `localFallback()` helper, so
181:    it is structurally impossible for template content to leave the gateway untagged.
182:    Callers respond according to what the content is *for*: `ask`/`chunk` record it in
183:    `Provenance.isLocalFallback` (so the card carries the truth permanently) and the receipt
184:    warns; the syllabus, query-suggestion, and cited-brief steps **refuse** outright, since
185:    a template syllabus would be confidently wrong about the goal and a "cited" brief that
186:    read no evidence is a contradiction.
187: 2. **Add `bun-types` to `tsconfig`** so `npx tsc --noEmit` is clean end-to-end and can
188:    become a CI gate.
189: 3. **Extend undo beyond one step**, using the persisted log that already supports it.
190: 4. **Revisit onboarding** — the PRD's cold-start four questions were never built, and
191:    missions are currently something you have to go and find.
</file>

